It includes code adapted from ReCaVSR (https://github.com/kopperx/ReCaVSR) by Xijun Wang, Xin Li, Suhang Yao, Zirui
Lang, Bingchen Li and Zhibo Chen, University of Science and Technology of China, licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (LICENSE-APACHE):

- recavsr/attention.py: ReCaVSR's windowed-attention Triton kernel (kernels/local_attention.py), forward only, with
  retuned tiles and a PyTorch fallback added.
- recavsr/flashdecoder.py: the LR-conditioned FlashDecoder (models/flashdecoder/), forward only, on ComfyUI's ops.
- recavsr/cache.py: the routed KV history and the rolling temporal RoPE (runtime/cache.py, runtime/rope.py), with an
  option to keep the history in RAM added.
- recavsr/dit.py, recavsr/session.py: reimplemented on ComfyUI's ops after the reference runtime's streaming step,
  block schedule, LQ preparation and colour corrections, keeping the released module names so the weights load as
  they are.

The transformer is Wan2.2 TI2V-5B (Alibaba Wan team, Apache License 2.0) with ReCaVSR's adapters merged in.

The model weights are not part of this repository:

- the transformer, prompt and FlashDecoder: https://huggingface.co/kopper/ReCaVSR, which states no licence
- the int8 ConvRot transformer: https://huggingface.co/PedroMarinhoDev/ReCaVSR-ComfyUI, converted from the above

The clips in assets/ are inputs 021 and 009 of ReCaVSR's real-world demo set (https://huggingface.co/anonyaa/ReCaVSR),
upscaled with these nodes.
